WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.252
- Still to this day,
I don't believe he beat it.

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:04.129
- You still don't think
he ran a 4.22?

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:08.133
Simms Schefter over here got all the scoop
on Antonio Brown.

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.969
Derek Carr and Odell Beckham Jr.
and Jon Gruden on your team?

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:12.846
- Wow.
- That'll sell tickets in Vegas in a hurry.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:17.517
♪♪♪

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.520
- Wild Card playoffs, we made it!

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.897
- We made it, baby!
- Seventeen weeks and it's the playoffs!

00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:26.192
The regular season starts now! But guess what?

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.610
- For the New England Patriots.
- Yeah.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:28.611
- It's their regular season.
- Man.

00:00:28.611 --> 00:00:30.739
We're gonna get to all the teams later in the show.

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:34.492
Allie, helping us figure out Chicago and Philadelphia.

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:36.202
We check in with Chris Johnson–
- Right.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.954
- Our good buddy.
- CJ2K!

00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:43.168
- But two teams that aren't even in the playoffs,
their wide receivers have taken over the news cycle.

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:43.752
- Yeah.

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:49.966
- First, Simms Schefter over here got all the scoop
on Antonio Brown and the Pittsburgh Steelers.

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:51.634
- Right.
- It sounds like a mess.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:54.137
- It does sound like a mess.
I don't think there's any doubt about that.

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:55.680
- And you got some scoop.
- I do have scoop.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.559
Talking to players, ex-players, other
people that work in the organization,

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:03.438
I've gotten the story from a number
of people. And I think the one thing–

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:04.647
- Yeah, what did you take away from all this?

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:08.401
- The biggest thing is that Antonio Brown
has had dysfunctional issues

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:13.114
within that organization for a while, whether it's being
late for meetings, or little things that we saw this week.

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:16.034
- Like, always late for meetings?
- Habitual. This is a habitual thing, right.

00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:20.121
- We've said this as people have
crucified Odell over the years that Antonio,

00:01:20.121 --> 00:01:24.417
from the Gatorade smashing, to the
Facebook Lives, to the insulting the reporter,

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.587
threatening the reporter–
- To furniture off the balcony.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.047
- Right, it's been constant.

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:31.257
- It has been constant, and–
- So we're not shocked.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:34.302
- No, we're not shocked. We have
heard all of these stories.

00:01:34.302 --> 00:01:36.888
I think what's shocking, last week,
and it was such a big game.

00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:40.183
They're playing to get into the playoffs,
hopefully, against the Cincinnati Bengals.

00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:43.103
There's a disagreement during
a walkthrough on Wednesday.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:48.942
Antonio Brown felt disrespected about it.
He didn't show up for at least two to three days.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:49.526
- Just didn't show up?

00:01:49.526 --> 00:01:53.488
- Didn't show up at all. And then came to
the locker room on Sunday expecting to play,

00:01:53.488 --> 00:01:55.698
and of course, they did not let him do that.

00:01:55.698 --> 00:02:01.162
And then he went out there, and you saw him in his mink coat.
And he's the man, don't get me wrong, he's a baller supreme.

00:02:01.162 --> 00:02:03.873
- Yes.
- But he did, yes. I was told he left at halftime.

00:02:03.873 --> 00:02:07.627
- Your big point is, whenever something happens on the Steelers,

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:10.797
we point a finger at Mike Tomlin and say he has no control.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.925
- Right.
- And you're saying, "Exactly. He has no control."

00:02:13.925 --> 00:02:15.135
- Thank you.
- "So why are we blaming Tomlin?"

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.970
- Exactly right. I don't like that Mike Tomlin

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:23.226
gets the blame for all of these things when, you know,
he's not the center focus of who drafted some of these players

00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:29.816
or negotiating their contracts, or negotiating to the
point where there's so much dead money right now.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.110
Then people go, "Well, they're gonna trade Antonio Brown."

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.320
No, they're not. They can't trade Antonio Brown.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.867
If they trade him or cut him, they are
gonna be on the hook for $21 million.

00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:42.287
That's like three or four quality
starting players on your roster.

00:02:42.287 --> 00:02:43.288
- Might as well keep him and try to win with him.

00:02:43.288 --> 00:02:46.583
- Exactly right, and deal with him.
You've been dealing with him already anyway.

00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:50.295
- In comparison, Odell seems like a choir boy.
- [Laughing] Yeah.

00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:53.756
- And a lot of people have been saying,
including you, they're gonna trade him.

00:02:53.756 --> 00:02:56.551
You don't got a quarterback that can
reach him. It doesn't make sense.

00:02:56.551 --> 00:02:58.845
Gettleman has come out and says,
"We're not gonna trade him."

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:01.222
- Right.
- But you don't say–

00:03:01.222 --> 00:03:05.268
- Well, it's early in the offseason. Ehh, I gotta see it to believe it there.
- Yeah.

00:03:05.268 --> 00:03:12.066
- I mean, yeah, I just think there's some things, you know,
reading the tea leaves or between the lines, right, of just what we've seen.

00:03:12.066 --> 00:03:16.779
First of all, I think in the Mara family, who's close to the
Rooney family in Pittsburgh, and they're probably goin',

00:03:16.779 --> 00:03:22.327
"Hmm, do we really want this issue to happen to us
two or three years down the road with Odell Beckham Jr. maybe?"

00:03:22.327 --> 00:03:25.079
- Interesting.
- To me, just thinking as a football person,

00:03:25.079 --> 00:03:28.958
and I know there'll be a demand for him,
and then a lot of his money's been paid already.

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:31.711
So then teams are gonna go,
"Ooh, well that's not so bad to trade for him."

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:35.465
I'm just saying, it's a possibility.
- Let's open up the Simms Chaos Generator.

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:39.844
- Oh, gosh.
- I'm gonna turn this wheel, and we're gonna
put out four teams that Odell could possibly go to.

00:03:39.844 --> 00:03:42.805
- Sure.
- We're gonna start off in Indianapolis.

00:03:42.805 --> 00:03:45.850
- Yes. Yes, the Indianapolis Colts.
They have so much money.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:49.812
You have an offensive line. You got,
of course, Andrew Luck, right?

00:03:49.812 --> 00:03:53.816
You don't– I don't think they need necessarily
to go out and get a big-time running back

00:03:53.816 --> 00:03:56.694
cuz they got two or three in the rotation that are good already.
- Yeah.

00:03:56.694 --> 00:04:01.699
- But you pair up an Odell Beckham Jr. with
Andrew Luck on the other side of T.Y. Hilton?

00:04:01.699 --> 00:04:06.537
Whoo! Watch out. That is a young nucleus
that could grow together and really be special.

00:04:06.537 --> 00:04:07.914
- I got another young quarterback for you.
- OK.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:12.001
- Crank, crank, crank, crank, crank. Josh Allen.
- Ooh, I mean, that to me–

00:04:12.001 --> 00:04:17.298
- I just wanna say that Odell in Buffalo is
not a visual that I thought I'd see.

00:04:17.298 --> 00:04:20.468
- I get it.
- He'd be out there in a mink coat bein' like, "Y'all live in this crap?"

00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:23.304
- [Laughing] Right.
- But Josh Allen throwing to Odell–

00:04:23.304 --> 00:04:28.393
- I think that's where I look at it–yes, the commercial
appeal is not gonna be there about the Buffalo Bills.

00:04:28.393 --> 00:04:31.104
But the New York Giants, if they are trading him away,

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:34.357
aren't gonna be worried about what his
commercial appeal is in this situation.

00:04:34.357 --> 00:04:36.401
But I look at a team like the Buffalo Bills–

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:39.487
have a lot of money, assets and then a quarterback

00:04:39.529 --> 00:04:44.325
and then a quarterback who has an arm like
Patrick Mahomes and big-time talent that we saw.

00:04:44.325 --> 00:04:47.328
- We'll see where it all ends up, but there's
no weapons there to support him right now,

00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:49.122
and I'm just sayin', that's one guy that could help.

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.873
- Last one.
- Bum-bum-bum-bum-bum.

00:04:50.873 --> 00:04:52.959
- Our favorite coach in the NFL.
- That's right.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:59.007
- Kyle Shanahan. We thought–you thought–maybe
the Niners before the contract got done.

00:04:59.007 --> 00:05:01.759
- Yeah. Well, I'm gonna throw another one in there with it.

00:05:01.759 --> 00:05:07.098
I'm gonna put the Bay Area in general. The Raiders
and the 49ers, I think, would be in this conversation.

00:05:07.098 --> 00:05:08.808
- Really?
- First of all, let's just talk about the Raiders.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:09.642
Going to Vegas, and you've got Derek Carr
and Odell Beckham Jr. and Jon Gruden on your team?

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:12.645
Going to Vegas, and you've got Derek Carr
and Odell Beckham Jr. and Jon Gruden on your team?

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.731
- Wow.
- That'll sell tickets in Vegas in a hurry, OK?

00:05:14.731 --> 00:05:15.148
- Wow.
- That'll sell tickets in Vegas in a hurry, OK?

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:18.901
And I just think they need the weapons,
and Jon Gruden can use him in that type of offense.

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:21.738
Same thing with Kyle Shanahan and the San Francisco 49ers.

00:05:21.738 --> 00:05:27.702
I think that could make sense and certainly make a splash
for the 49ers to go, "Here we come for our playoff run in 2019."

00:05:27.702 --> 00:05:33.458
- Le'Veon, Odell and Antonio all go to the Colts.
- [Laughing]

00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:35.918
- And Andrew Luck has a field day in 2019!

00:05:35.918 --> 00:05:38.254
- Throws for 75 touchdown passes.
- Incredible.

00:05:39.589 --> 00:05:41.007
Hi, I'm Champ Bailey,

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:42.925
and you're watching
Simms &amp; Lefkoe.

00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:46.429
- Usually I do
the introductions, but I—

00:05:46.429 --> 00:05:48.056
This is you.
This is your guy.

00:05:48.056 --> 00:05:49.390
- This is my guy.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:52.935
I mean, this is
the original CJ2K.

00:05:52.935 --> 00:05:54.395
My man right here.

00:05:54.395 --> 00:05:56.230
I didn't know what to expect
when I saw

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:57.774
this guy in person as a player.
Like—

00:05:57.774 --> 00:05:59.150
- Cuz he was a rookie
when you were there.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.943
- He was a rookie.

00:06:00.943 --> 00:06:03.029
And in training camp, I was
with the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.531
So I—
that team, as he'll tell you

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.825
had a bunch of Texas guys
on the Tennessee Titans team.

00:06:07.825 --> 00:06:09.911
And they kept telling me,
"Man, this Chris Johnson

00:06:09.911 --> 00:06:11.162
is a baller, man.

00:06:11.162 --> 00:06:12.747
We've never seen
anybody so fast."

00:06:12.747 --> 00:06:14.874
And I was like,
"Yeah, bleh, bleh, bleh, bleh."

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.835
But then I got there and

00:06:17.835 --> 00:06:21.130
yes, one of the most special
talents I have ever been around.

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:23.216
- And then, your memories
of Chris Simms back then?

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:26.177
- Oh, man. He used to talk trash
to me before every game.

00:06:26.177 --> 00:06:27.887
- Stop.
- I think it was probably

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.097
like Week 2 or Week 3.

00:06:29.097 --> 00:06:30.723
He was like, "Ah, come on"

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.393
I was—I think I had went
for 100 yards, like, twice.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:34.894
He's like, "Come on, man.

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:37.188
I'm tired of seeing these 10-,
15-yard runs.

00:06:37.188 --> 00:06:38.648
Break off somethin' long."

00:06:38.648 --> 00:06:41.275
I think, that same game,
LenDale broke for 80

00:06:41.275 --> 00:06:43.528
and I came right back
and broke for, like, 76.

00:06:43.528 --> 00:06:44.946
- Kansas City.
- Kansas City.

00:06:44.946 --> 00:06:46.739
- Kansas City game.
He did.

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:49.033
- I feel like that's when the
Smash and Dash thing took off.

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:50.326
- Right. It did.

00:06:50.326 --> 00:06:51.619
- When those two big
runs happened.

00:06:51.619 --> 00:06:53.121
- Yeah.
- Yep.

00:06:53.121 --> 00:06:54.956
- I think that's
a nickname that I feel like

00:06:54.956 --> 00:06:57.166
they try to give
to a lot of duos now.

00:06:57.166 --> 00:06:58.584
But you guys
were Smash and Dash.

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.002
- Yeah, yeah, we started that.

00:07:00.002 --> 00:07:02.171
They asked us, like,
what was our name.

00:07:02.171 --> 00:07:03.756
-Yes.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:05.299
- And LenDale was like,
"We Smash and Dash."

00:07:05.299 --> 00:07:06.759
- Right.
- He came up with Smash and Dash

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.177
and then ever since then

00:07:08.177 --> 00:07:10.179
they just started
calling us that every week.

00:07:10.179 --> 00:07:11.639
- Smash and Dash, OK

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:13.891
him and LenDale,
I mean, characters

00:07:13.891 --> 00:07:15.810
and LenDale
especially a character.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:18.062
- That's an all-time
running back room.

00:07:18.062 --> 00:07:19.230
- Yeah.
- Yes.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.232
And LenDale—

00:07:21.232 --> 00:07:24.235
we can put him on blast now
cuz his career is over—

00:07:24.235 --> 00:07:27.238
- [Laughing]
- He was late a lot, OK?

00:07:27.238 --> 00:07:29.532
I mean, late a lot.
- Right.

00:07:29.532 --> 00:07:32.410
- Like, and always had
a different excuse.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.162
Creative as hell, right?

00:07:34.162 --> 00:07:36.205
- How much is "late"?
- Yeah, see? He knows it's true.

00:07:36.205 --> 00:07:38.416
Like, if we had an 8:30 meeting

00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:41.627
LenDale was, I felt like,
never there at 8:30.

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:43.588
Never.
- And this is every day?

00:07:43.588 --> 00:07:45.089
- I mean, at least once
or twice a week.

00:07:45.089 --> 00:07:46.424
- OK.

00:07:46.424 --> 00:07:48.801
- And he'd always have
some great excuse.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.219
I mean, great.

00:07:50.219 --> 00:07:51.762
What do you think
his best excuse was?

00:07:51.762 --> 00:07:54.056
What was one you remember,
you remember any good ones?

00:07:54.056 --> 00:07:58.060
- Yeah. He was late one time,
and he came in and he was like

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:02.064
"Man, I had to pull over
to the gas station bathroom

00:08:02.064 --> 00:08:03.566
and my stomach was hurting.

00:08:03.566 --> 00:08:05.568
I had to use the bathroom."
- He was just—

00:08:05.568 --> 00:08:08.237
So his excuse was "I took a crap
at a gas station."

00:08:08.237 --> 00:08:10.239
- I had to take a crap
in a bathroom, yes.

00:08:10.239 --> 00:08:13.201
- And then when he says that,
the team explodes?

00:08:13.201 --> 00:08:15.870
- No, actually.
Cuz it's a serious setting.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.413
- [Laughing]
- I mean, we're all shaking
our head like

00:08:17.413 --> 00:08:18.956
"What a bunch of bullcrap
that is."

00:08:18.956 --> 00:08:20.416
But there's nothin' we can say

00:08:20.416 --> 00:08:21.918
cuz Jeff Fisher is still
the head coach

00:08:21.918 --> 00:08:23.419
and he's standing
in front of the room

00:08:23.419 --> 00:08:24.545
and we're not gonna butt
into that conversation.

00:08:24.545 --> 00:08:25.004
and we're not gonna butt
into that conversation.

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:25.838
So I want to ask Mr. 4.24

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:27.006
So I want to ask Mr. 4.24

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:29.717
who's the fastest guy
in the NFL right now?

00:08:29.717 --> 00:08:31.093
- Tyreek Hill.
- OK.

00:08:31.093 --> 00:08:32.553
- Gotta go with Tyreek Hill.

00:08:32.553 --> 00:08:34.388
- Is it unreal how fast he is?
- He's fast.

00:08:34.388 --> 00:08:36.891
- I mean, like, I'm not tryin'
to disrespect you

00:08:36.891 --> 00:08:38.643
or Joey Galloway
or Deion Sanders

00:08:38.643 --> 00:08:41.729
but he is the fastest f--ker
I have ever seen.

00:08:41.729 --> 00:08:43.814
- Maybe he's the second-
or the third-fastest.

00:08:43.814 --> 00:08:45.191
I wouldn't say the fastest.

00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:46.651
- You wouldn't say
he's the fastest?
- Not the fastest.

00:08:46.651 --> 00:08:48.110
- I know, cuz you're gonna
take yourself.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:49.779
- Of course.
- I know.

00:08:49.779 --> 00:08:52.114
- Of course.
- You should.

00:08:52.114 --> 00:08:56.077
- What was bigger,
the 2,000 or the 4.24?

00:08:56.077 --> 00:08:57.870
- 2,000.
- Mm.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.830
But the 4.24 we had
never seen before.

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:01.499
You got the watch made,
all that.

00:09:01.499 --> 00:09:02.833
- Yeah.

00:09:02.833 --> 00:09:05.002
- When you saw John Ross
beat the 4.24—

00:09:05.002 --> 00:09:06.879
- Eye emoji.

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:09.298
That was what he sent out, as
soon as he ran the—remember?

00:09:09.298 --> 00:09:11.008
The official time hadn't came in

00:09:11.008 --> 00:09:12.593
and he tweeted "eye emoji,"
the big eyes.

00:09:12.593 --> 00:09:14.303
- Was there part of you
that was like

00:09:14.303 --> 00:09:17.348
"I hope that gets corrected
and it's actually a 4.25."

00:09:17.348 --> 00:09:19.016
- Probably a part of me.

00:09:19.016 --> 00:09:22.353
But still to this day,
I don't believe he beat it.

00:09:22.353 --> 00:09:23.980
- You still don't think
he ran a 4.22?

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.565
- No.
When you look—

00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:28.943
OK, for one, when you look
at the side-by-side

00:09:28.943 --> 00:09:29.485
OK, for one, when you look
at the side-by-side

00:09:29.485 --> 00:09:31.070
I pulled off on him
at the end.

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.072
- Right.
- That's fascinating.

00:09:33.072 --> 00:09:36.492
- And number two is,
when has it ever took

00:09:36.492 --> 00:09:38.202
that long for the official time
to come in?

00:09:38.202 --> 00:09:40.204
- It did take a long time.
You're right.

00:09:40.204 --> 00:09:41.455
- Wow.

00:09:41.455 --> 00:09:43.749
- So you believe
that it was rigged?

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:45.376
Just say it.
Say it with your chest.

00:09:45.376 --> 00:09:47.044
- They probably got tired of,
tired of—

00:09:47.044 --> 00:09:48.713
- Showing your highlight
all the time?

00:09:48.713 --> 00:09:50.548
- Yeah, they probably got tired
of no one beating it

00:09:50.548 --> 00:09:52.717
and felt like the combine
was getting boring, so—

00:09:52.717 --> 00:09:54.135
- Right.
- They needed more attention.

00:09:54.135 --> 00:09:55.469
- Needed more attention.
- I love it.

00:09:55.469 --> 00:09:56.887
- I'm a big
conspiracy theory guy.

00:09:56.887 --> 00:09:58.222
This is one of the best ones
I've ever heard.

00:09:58.222 --> 00:10:00.182
